   "author": "de1d27fecc0bbd03",
   "date": "2018-04-01T02:53:37Z",
   "subject": "K-multiv",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hello everyone, <br><br>I am trying to assess the presence of phylogenetic signal in shape data using K-multiv. However, I am obtaining extremely low values of K (0.003) but with significant p-values. Of course, values close to 0 indicate the absene of phylogenetic signal but they are extremely low. Also happens with size data.<br>I wonder if this make sense in terms of no phylogenetic signal. Thanks in advance!<br>B-<br><br>PS.shape &lt;- physignal(A=gdf2$Y3,phy=mytree,iter=9999, print.progress = TRUE)<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bO7x0HbnBgAJ",
   "from": "Antigoni Kaliontzopoulou",
   "author": "511e44c7d1e1bab0",
   "date": "2018-04-01T09:49:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] K-multiv",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    <p>Borja,</p>\r\n    <p>the randomizations to assess phylogenetic signal using K evaluate\r\n      whether there is, or not, an association between (multivariate, in\r\n      the generalization of the method) phenotype and phylogeny under a\r\n      BM process, where the expected value of K=1. These randomizations\r\n      do NOT assess the hypothesis of K=1 or K=0 or any other value, or\r\n      deviations from it. And K=0 does not mean absence of phylogenetic\r\n      signal, but rather a strong deviation from what phenotypic\r\n      variation would look like under BM. <br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>A detailed treatment about the original implementation of the\r\n      method, null hypotheses tested and the meaning of values of K can\r\n      be found in <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\">Blomberg SP, Garland T, Ives AR. 2003. Testing for\r\n        phylogenetic signal in comparative data: behavioral traits are\r\n        more labile. Evolution, 57:717-745, but read also the paper on\r\n        the multivariate generalization into detail (</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\">Adams, D.C.\r\n          2014. A generalized K statistic for estimating phylogenetic\r\n          signal from shape and other high-dimensional multivariate\r\n          data. Systematic Biology. 63:685-697.). I think both will help\r\n          you with interpretingthe values you are getting.</span></span></p>\r\n    <p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\">Hope this helps</span></span></p>\r\n    <p><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.333333015441895px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;float:none\">Antigoni<br>\r\n        </span></span></p></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 01/04/2018 03:53, Boficas wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div>"
